From aa64342a9e13affffea3e989d67e574475af5a78 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Roland Shoemaker <bracewell@google.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 14:20:28 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] crypto/x509: distrust a handful of intermediates

Backport https://go-review.googlesource.com/c/go/+/851145, patch set 2
(aa64342a9e13affffea3e989d67e574475af5a78), to Go 1.21.

Filter chains containing any of the upstream SHA-256 SPKI hashes in both
the Go and platform verifiers, including ExtKeyUsageAny and directly
trusted certificates. Keep alternative chains which do not contain a
distrusted key.

Go 1.21 has neither slices.DeleteFunc nor the NoValidChains error reason.
Use explicit filtering loops and UnknownAuthorityError when distrust
eliminates all chains, without adding a public API to this release.
Keep the existing key-usage error when otherwise trusted chains fail EKU
checks, and preserve the Windows highest-quality-context error.

The upstream change contains no tests. Add regression tests for chain
positions, reissued certificates, alternative paths, direct trust, EKU
bypasses, and platform verification where system trust is available.
SHA-256 uses crypto/sha256, preserving the fork's OpenSSL dispatch.

Fixes CVE-2026-111943
For golang/go#82345
For golang/go#82348
---

diff --git a/src/crypto/x509/verify.go b/src/crypto/x509/verify.go
--- a/src/crypto/x509/verify.go
